{#-
  The decoy cover page.

  Rendered once per page in the site's `pages` list, plus a 404. The home page
  (slug `index`) gets the full landing-page treatment: hero, intro, services,
  call to action, testimonials, mission, location and contact. Inner pages get
  the header, a content card and the footer, because a real small site has one
  designed page and several plainer ones, and a site where every page is a
  showcase is the one that looks generated.

  Pictures come from one of two places, and every slot falls back to the other.

  Photographs are fetched by THIS HOST at deploy time and served from its own
  docroot (see files/rsp-decoy-fetch.py). Drawn SVG, generated at compile time
  by redstackpro.decoyart, fills any slot that has no photograph.

  What the page never does is reach a third party while it is being served. No
  CDN, no web font, no analytics, no tracking pixel: a visitor's browser talks
  only to this host, so nothing tells anyone else the redirector's hostname in a
  Referer, and no image breaks the day some other host is blocked. Because each
  redirector fetches its own photographs from its own seed and re-encodes them,
  there is still no asset hash that identifies a redStackPRO cover page.
  See 0041, decoyart.py and decoyassets.py.

  The contact form posts to itself and the server has nothing behind it, so the
  method is GET and the action is the current page: a submit reloads the page
  rather than producing an error, which is the quietest way for a form with no
  backend to behave.
-#}
{#- Which photographs actually landed. Set by the role after the fetch; empty
    when the decoy is off, when the host has no egress, or on any slot the
    search could not fill. Every use below is guarded, so an empty map renders
    exactly the page the drawn artwork rendered before photographs existed. -#}
{% set photo = redstackpro_decoy_images | default({}, true) -%}
{#- Every lookup below goes through .get(), and the reason is not style.
    `photo.slot` on a plain dict returns Undefined when the key is absent,
    which is falsy, so `{% if photo.slot %}` reads as false and the drawn
    fallback renders -- under plain Jinja. Ansible's templating raises
    instead: "object of type 'dict' has no attribute 'video'", which fails
    the task and the whole deploy.

    That difference makes the missing-slot path -- the one this design is
    built on, where every slot is optional -- the path that breaks in
    production and works everywhere it is tested. It surfaced on the first
    live deploy, on the video slot, because that is the slot nothing fills
    without an operator pack. Every other slot had the same defect latent in
    it, waiting for a search that returned nothing. -#}
{% set hero_photo = photo.get('hero') -%}
{% set hero_clip = photo.get('video') -%}
{% set intro_photo = photo.get('intro') -%}
{#- What a tel: link dials, as opposed to what the page shows. A displayed
    number wants the brackets and the dash a reader expects -- (503) 311-0148,
    or 0113 496 0139 -- and a dialable one must not carry them. Derived rather
    than stored twice, so the two can never drift apart, and stripped with
    chained replaces rather than a regex because Ansible's regex_replace is not
    a Jinja builtin and this template is also rendered by plain Jinja in the
    tests. -#}
{% set telephone = sections.phone | default('', true) | replace(' ', '')
                   | replace('(', '') | replace(')', '') | replace('-', '') -%}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>{{ page.heading }} - {{ site.brand }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ site.tagline }}">
<style>
:root {
  --bg: {{ site.bg }};
  --card: {{ site.card }};
  --accent: {{ site.accent }};
  --text: {{ site.text }};
  --muted: {{ site.muted }};
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { font-family: {{ site.font | default("'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif") }};
       background: var(--bg); color: var(--muted); margin: 0; min-height: 100vh;
       display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 1.6; }
a { color: inherit; }
.wrap { width: 100%; max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }

header { background: var(--card); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
         position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 5; }
.bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
       gap: 16px; padding: 14px 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; text-decoration: none; }
.brand svg { width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: 10px; display: block; }
.brand-name { color: var(--text); font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.2px; }
nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; margin-left: 20px; font-size: 14px; }
nav a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
.call { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; padding: 9px 17px; border-radius: 7px;
        font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; }

main { flex: 1; width: 100%; }
section { padding: 60px 0; }
h1 { color: var(--text); font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
h2 { color: var(--text); font-size: 26px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
h3 { color: var(--text); font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 7px; }
p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
.lede { font-size: 17px; max-width: 62ch; }

.hero { position: relative; padding: 0; }
.hero-art { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }
.hero-art svg, .hero-art img { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; object-fit: cover; }
/* A slow drift across the hero photograph, which is the cheapest way to have
   a moving hero: no clip to source, no licence to satisfy, nothing extra in
   the export, and it rides the photograph the host already fetched, so it
   stays different per deployment for free.

   Both ends scale ABOVE 1 on purpose. At scale 1 the image exactly fills the
   band, so any translate at all drags an edge into view and the hero shows a
   strip of background. The smaller end keeps 3% of overflow in hand and the
   translate is well inside it. */
@keyframes hero-drift {
  from { transform: scale(1.06) translate3d(0, 0, 0); }
  to   { transform: scale(1.34) translate3d(-4%, -2.5%, 0); }
}
/* LINEAR, and that matters more than the numbers. ease-in-out on an infinite
   alternate animation brings the velocity to zero at BOTH ends and holds it
   near zero for seconds either side, so whether the hero appears to move at
   all depends on when somebody happens to look at it. Constant velocity reads
   as continuous motion at a rate that a peak-velocity figure flatters.

   The span was raised twice, because "is it animating" is the wrong question
   and every test asking it passed on a drift nobody could see. */
.hero-art img { animation: hero-drift 18s linear infinite alternate; }
/* The clip sits ON TOP of whichever still was going to fill the hero, rather
   than replacing it. That still is the poster, so the band is never empty
   while the video buffers, and a browser that declines to autoplay shows a
   finished hero instead of a black rectangle. */
.hero-video { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;
              object-fit: cover; display: block; }
/* Honouring reduced motion is not only courtesy here. A site that ignores the
   preference is a site built carelessly, and the cover page is trying to read
   as one somebody maintains. Hiding the clip uncovers the still underneath. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .hero-video { display: none; }
  .hero-art img { animation: none; }
}
/* The drawn hero is a dark gradient by construction, so white headline text
   always reads on it. A photograph carries no such guarantee -- a bright sky
   behind white type is unreadable -- so a photographic hero gets a scrim. */
.scrim { position: absolute; inset: 0;
         background: linear-gradient(105deg,
                     rgba(0,0,0,0.68) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.46) 52%, rgba(0,0,0,0.24) 100%); }
.hero-inner { position: relative; padding: 86px 0 92px; }
.hero h1, .hero p { color: #fff; }
.hero h1 { max-width: 20ch; }
.hero p { max-width: 54ch; opacity: 0.94; font-size: 17px; }
.btn { display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; background: #fff; color: var(--accent);
       padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 7px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }

.split { display: flex; gap: 46px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.split > div { flex: 1 1 320px; min-width: 0; }
.figure { border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 6px 22px rgba(0,0,0,0.10); }
.figure svg, .figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

.grid { display: flex; gap: 22px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.grid > * { flex: 1 1 260px; min-width: 0; }
.card { background: var(--card); border-radius: 12px; padding: 26px 28px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); }
.card svg { width: 44px; height: 44px; display: block; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.card p { font-size: 14px; margin: 0; }
/* A card with a photograph puts it edge to edge at the top and moves the
   padding inside, the way a service card on a real site is built. A card with
   a drawn glyph keeps the original padded layout. */
.card-shot { padding: 0; overflow: hidden; }
.card-shot .shot { width: 100%; height: 168px; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
.card-shot .card-body { padding: 22px 26px 26px; }

.cta { background: var(--accent); border-radius: 14px; padding: 34px 38px;
       display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
       gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.cta h2, .cta p { color: #fff; margin: 0; }
.cta p { opacity: 0.92; font-size: 15px; }
.cta .btn { margin: 0; }

.quote { background: var(--card); border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px 26px;
         box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); }
.quote p { font-size: 14px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text); }
.who { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; margin-top: 14px; }
.who svg, .who .face { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; display: block;
                       flex: none; object-fit: cover; }
.credits { padding-left: 20px; margin: 14px 0 0; }
.credits li { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 7px; }
.who b { color: var(--text); font-size: 14px; display: block; font-weight: 600; }
.who span { font-size: 12px; }

.mission { position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 14px; }
.mission-art { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
.mission-art svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
.mission-inner { position: relative; padding: 44px 46px; }
.mission h2, .mission p { color: #fff; }
.mission p { max-width: 62ch; opacity: 0.93; margin: 0; }

.stats { display: flex; gap: 22px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.stat { flex: 1 1 180px; text-align: center; }
.stat b { display: block; color: var(--accent); font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; }
.stat span { font-size: 13px; }

.field { display: block; margin-bottom: 13px; }
.field span { display: block; font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 5px; color: var(--text); }
.field input, .field textarea {
  width: 100%; padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.16);
  border-radius: 7px; font: inherit; font-size: 14px; background: #fff; color: var(--text); }
.field textarea { min-height: 96px; resize: vertical; }
button.send { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border: 0; padding: 11px 24px;
              border-radius: 7px; font: inherit; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }
.contact-detail { font-size: 14px; }
.contact-detail b { color: var(--text); }

footer { background: var(--card); border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
         padding: 40px 0 26px; margin-top: 20px; }
.foot { display: flex; gap: 40px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; }
.foot h4 { color: var(--text); font-size: 13px; margin: 0 0 9px; text-transform: uppercase;
           letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
.foot a, .foot p { display: block; font-size: 13px; text-decoration: none; margin: 0 0 6px; }
.foot a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
.legal { border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.07); margin-top: 26px; padding-top: 18px;
         font-size: 12px; opacity: 0.75; }
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  h1 { font-size: 29px; }
  .hero-inner { padding: 60px 0; }
  .mission-inner { padding: 32px 26px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="wrap bar">
    <a class="brand" href="/">{{ art.logo }}<span class="brand-name">{{ site.brand }}</span></a>
    <nav>
    {%- for p in site.pages %}
      <a href="{{ '/' if p.slug == 'index' else '/' ~ p.slug ~ '.html' }}">{{ p.label }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
    <a class="call" href="tel:{{ telephone }}">{{ sections.phone }}</a>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
{#- .get() again, and for the same reason as the photographs above: the
    404 page is built from the catalog's `notfound` block, which carries no
    slug because it is not a navigable page. `page.slug` is falsy-Undefined
    under plain Jinja and raises under Ansible, so the 404 -- the page a
    scanner is most likely to see -- was the one page that could not be
    written. Only `slug` is optional; heading and body are guaranteed by the
    catalog, and reaching for .get() on those would hide a real defect. -#}
{% if page.get('slug') == 'index' %}

  {# 1. Hero. Three layers, deepest first, each one the fallback for the one
     above it: drawn artwork always works, a photograph covers it when one was
     found, and a clip covers that when the operator supplied one. Nothing here
     depends on the layer above existing, which is why a blocked egress, an
     empty search and an absent pack all still render a finished band. #}
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-art">
      {%- if hero_photo %}<img src="/assets/{{ hero_photo }}" alt="">
      {%- else %}{{ art.hero }}{% endif %}
      {%- if hero_clip %}
      {#- muted is what makes autoplay permitted at all, and is what an
          unremarkable business site would do regardless; playsinline stops a
          phone taking the page over with a fullscreen player. #}
      <video class="hero-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"
             {%- if hero_photo %} poster="/assets/{{ hero_photo }}"{% endif %}>
        <source src="/assets/{{ hero_clip }}"
                type="video/{{ 'webm' if hero_clip.endswith('.webm') else 'mp4' }}">
      </video>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if hero_photo or hero_clip %}<div class="scrim"></div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <h1>{{ page.heading }}</h1>
      <p>{{ page.body[0] }}</p>
      <a class="btn" href="#contact">{{ sections.cta.heading }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# 2. Intro, alongside a figure #}
  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>{{ site.tagline }}</h2>
        {% for para in page.body[1:] %}<p class="lede">{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
        <p class="lede">{{ sections.hours }}</p>
      </div>
      {# A photograph if one landed; otherwise the drawn street grid, which is
         why the map is generated and not fetched from a tile server. #}
      <div class="figure">
        {%- if intro_photo %}<img src="/assets/{{ intro_photo }}" alt="">
        {%- else %}{{ art.map }}{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 3. Services #}
  <section style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.02);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <div class="grid" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        {% for service in sections.services %}
        {%- set shot = photo.get('service-' ~ loop.index0) %}
        <div class="card{% if shot %} card-shot{% endif %}">
          {%- if shot %}<img class="shot" src="/assets/{{ shot }}" alt="">
          {%- else %}{{ art.icons[loop.index0 % art.icons | length] }}{% endif %}
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>{{ service.title }}</h3>
            <p>{{ service.body }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 4. Call to action #}
  <section style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div>
          <h2>{{ sections.cta.heading }}</h2>
          <p>{{ sections.cta.body }}</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn" href="tel:{{ telephone }}">{{ sections.phone }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 5. Testimonials #}
  <section style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What people say</h2>
      <div class="grid" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        {% for person in sections.testimonials %}
        <div class="quote">
          <p>{{ person.quote }}</p>
          <div class="who">
            {%- set face = photo.get('face-' ~ loop.index0) %}
            {%- if face %}<img class="face" src="/assets/{{ face }}" alt="">
            {%- else %}{{ art.avatars[loop.index0 % art.avatars | length] }}{% endif %}
            <span><b>{{ person.name }}</b><span>{{ person.role }}</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 6. Mission #}
  <section style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="mission">
        <div class="mission-art">{{ art.band }}</div>
        <div class="mission-inner">
          <h2>{{ sections.mission.heading }}</h2>
          <p>{{ sections.mission.body }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 7. Statistics #}
  <section>
    <div class="wrap stats">
      {% for stat in sections.stats %}
      <div class="stat"><b>{{ stat.value }}</b><span>{{ stat.label }}</span></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 8. Location and 9. contact form #}
  <section id="contact" style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.02);">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Find us</h2>
        <p class="contact-detail">
          {% for line in sections.address %}<b>{{ line }}</b><br>{% endfor %}
        </p>
        <p class="contact-detail">{{ sections.hours }}</p>
        <p class="contact-detail">Telephone <b>{{ sections.phone }}</b></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <form method="get" action="">
          <label class="field"><span>Name</span><input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name"></label>
          <label class="field"><span>Email</span><input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email"></label>
          <label class="field"><span>Message</span><textarea name="message"></textarea></label>
          <button class="send" type="submit">Send message</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

{% else %}

  {# An inner page: header, one card, footer. #}
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card" style="padding: 40px 44px;">
        <h1 style="font-size: 27px;">{{ page.heading }}</h1>
        {% for para in page.body %}<p>{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
        {%- if page.get('slug') == 'credits' %}
        {# Where a CC-BY photograph's attribution is discharged. It is here
           rather than on the cover because a credit line on a landing page is
           a tell; a credits page is what an ordinary small site has. Each
           entry names the photographer and the licence, and for a ShareAlike
           work that naming is also what puts the cropped version under the
           same terms. #}
        <p>Photography on this site is used under the licences shown.</p>
        <ul class="credits">
          {%- for credit in redstackpro_decoy_credits %}
          <li>{{ credit.title or 'Photograph' }} &mdash; {{ credit.artist }},
            {% if credit.url %}<a href="{{ credit.url }}" rel="nofollow noopener">{{ credit.licence }}</a>
            {%- else %}{{ credit.licence }}{% endif %}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

{% endif %}
</main>

{# 10. Footer #}
<footer>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="foot">
      <div style="flex: 1 1 260px;">
        {# logo_footer, not logo: identical artwork with a different gradient
           id, because the same id twice in one document is invalid and every
           reference resolves to whichever came first. #}
        <a class="brand" href="/" style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
          {{ art.logo_footer }}<span class="brand-name">{{ site.brand }}</span>
        </a>
        <p>{{ site.tagline }}</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Pages</h4>
        {%- for p in site.pages %}
        <a href="{{ '/' if p.slug == 'index' else '/' ~ p.slug ~ '.html' }}">{{ p.label }}</a>
        {%- endfor %}
        {#- Only when something is owed, so the site never links to a page that
            was not written. #}
        {%- if redstackpro_decoy_credits | default([], true) %}
        <a href="/credits.html">Credits</a>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Contact</h4>
        <a href="tel:{{ telephone }}">{{ sections.phone }}</a>
        {% for line in sections.address %}<p>{{ line }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Hours</h4>
        <p>{{ sections.hours }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="legal">&copy; {{ site.brand }} &middot; {{ site.tagline }}</div>
  </div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
